# Study data. Never committed, to any repository, private or otherwise.
# These are human subject exports held under the terms they were collected
# under, and a git history keeps a copy even after a file is deleted.
data/

# Secrets: API keys, the session secret, and the cluster host.
# The example file is the template and carries placeholders, so it stays.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
clients/.env

# Results, and everything derived from a run. Large, regenerable, and often
# holding study data in another shape.
clients/outputs/
outputs/
.retired/

# Chats, conversations, run registries, and per-user state. One person's
# transcript is not something another may read, so none of it goes anywhere a
# second person could reach it.
clients/.userdata/
.userdata/

# Built environments. Hundreds of megabytes, and specific to the machine that
# built them. The manifests that describe them are committed; the trees are not.
#
# Named one at a time on purpose. This was `**/environments/`, which matched the
# whole directory and so excluded restore.sh, requirements.txt and every lock
# file beside the tree as well — the recipes, not just what they build. The
# comment above was already the intention; the rule did not implement it, and
# `git status` stayed clean the whole time it was wrong. A clone could not
# rebuild any environment, and six capabilities were unavailable with no way to
# make them available.
#
# What a restore produces:
**/environments/py/
**/environments/*/renv/library/
**/environments/biobakery_workflows/
# A third-party binary fetched rather than built (see add_gotree_to_julia.sh).
**/environments/bin/
clients/.venv/
.venv/

# Reference datasets. Public, large, and installed rather than carried: a site
# profile names where each one lives (see `references` in infrastructure/sites).
domains/spatial-transcriptomics/reference/

# Study data by shape, wherever it lands. The rules above name the directories
# data is supposed to live in; this catches a file that ends up somewhere else,
# which is the case the directory rules cannot see. Nothing the product needs is
# one of these formats, so a match is always something that should not be here.
*.h5
*.h5ad
*.loom
*.rds
*.rda
*.RData
*.mtx
*.mtx.gz
*.bam
*.bai
*.cram
*.sam
*.fastq
*.fq
*.fastq.gz
*.fq.gz
*.vcf
*.vcf.gz
*.bcf
*.nii
*.nii.gz
*.parquet
*.feather
*.npy
*.npz
*.pkl
*.pickle

# Container images and archives. Built or downloaded, never carried.
*.sif
*.simg
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.zip

# Scheduler and run output picked up from a working directory.
*.log
slurm-*.out
*_[0-9]*.out
*_[0-9]*.err

# Editors and interpreters
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.DS_Store
.ipynb_checkpoints/
node_modules/
.vscode/
.idea/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
